WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.457
Hi, I'm Rutabaga!

00:00:02.457 --> 00:00:05.958
A looped Transformer runs one block over and over.

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:07.903
Depth costs compute, not parameters.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:12.760
The idea: store a few layers, run them many times, and feed

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.842
each pass back in.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.463
The prelude embeds the tokens once, into a vector e.

00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:26.208
Each pass, the core reads its last state together with e.

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:27.115
That's input injection.

00:00:28.113 --> 00:00:31.862
Its output becomes the next state, and the same four layers run again.

00:00:33.148 --> 00:00:37.393
After the last pass, the coda reads the state out as a next-token prediction.

00:00:38.858 --> 00:00:39.716
Count the cost.

00:00:40.858 --> 00:00:44.631
The core's weights are stored once, but every token uses them r times.

00:00:45.051 --> 00:00:46.783
The prelude and coda run once.

00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:52.970
At thirty-two passes, Huginn does the work of a fifty billion parameter

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.473
model, from three and a half billion stored.

00:00:57.692 --> 00:00:58.981
Training has its own trick.

00:01:00.003 --> 00:01:03.404
Sample how many passes to run, around thirty-two on average.

00:01:03.824 --> 00:01:04.983
Run them all forward.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:10.325
Backpropagate through only the last eight, so memory doesn't grow with depth.

00:01:10.745 --> 00:01:13.713
The prelude still learns, because e enters every pass.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.553
A fixed count is simple.

00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:19.920
But it spends the same on every token, and LOTUS gets worse

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.322
run past its training depth.

00:01:21.742 --> 00:01:26.146
Halting lets easy tokens stop early: a learned score in the Universal

00:01:26.146 --> 00:01:29.081
Transformer, or Huginn stopping once two passes agree.

00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:32.857
A loop turns depth into a compute budget.

00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:35.886
You pay in FLOPs, latency and cache, never in weights.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:42.321
A shared core between a prelude and a coda.

00:01:42.321 --> 00:01:43.546
The input, every pass.

00:01:43.546 --> 00:01:45.076
Backprop through the last few.

00:01:45.496 --> 00:01:47.754
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:47.754 --> 00:01:48.399
I'm Rutabaga.

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:48.722
Bye!
